 caller of a shared safety predicate) captured in an ADR / AGENTS.md"],"finding":"The plan extends scratch-volume enforcement to a new caller (the review-bot clone path) beyond where ADR 0112 places it (gate_admission wrapping plan-review/completion-verifier), but names no ADR/doc update recording that the review-bot clone path now shares the gate. This is a new architectural fact about the enforcement surface.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fed4e76dc98506cef","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 1-2; File impact","norm_id":"ndec3d56adac267db","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer reads ADR 0112, believes gate_admission is the sole enforcement point, and refactors the review-bot clone assuming it is unguarded"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an ADR 0112 addendum (and a File-impact entry for it) stating: refusal enforcement now spans two callers — gate_admission._require_scratch_volume and voter._decision_for_review_target — both reading gate_admission.scratch_unavailable_detail().","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Reconcile the review-bot clone's target volume (tempfile.gettempdir() via review_clone_has_room / TemporaryDirectory) with gate_admission's scratch-marker root (peek_store_root() = resolve_gate_tmpdir() or gettempdir()): state that the shared predicate resolves markers from the same filesystem the clone writes to, or point the clone's dir= at that root.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'It is a plain tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\") in voter._decision_for_review_target, following TMPDIR.'","gate_admission._require_scratch_volume: 'base = peek_store_root().parent'; peek_store_root() = 'config.resolve_gate_tmpdir() or tempfile.gettempdir()'","low_disk.review_clone_has_room calls has_min_free_space(tempfile.gettempdir()) — the clone volume is gettempdir(), not necessarily resolve_gate_tmpdir()"],"finding":"The plan reuses gate_admission's scratch predicate (rooted at peek_store_root() = resolve_gate_tmpdir() or gettempdir()) to gate a review-bot clone that the plan itself says 'follows TMPDIR' via tempfile.TemporaryDirectory / low_disk.review_clone_has_room (tempfile.gettempdir()). When REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR points at the dedicated volume but the review clone writes to a plain TMPDIR, the shared predicate refuses based on a filesystem the clone does not use — and conversely the clone can still land on root while the predicate's markers describe a different path. The plan does not reconcile the two path derivations, so the guard may not actually protect the directory the review clone writes to.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f386a490770555354","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1-2; _decision_for_review_target / low_disk.review_clone_has_room","norm_id":"ncfebdcc3e899616b","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Ho